{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:033H:title", "parent_tag": "033H", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "section_title", "risk_level": "R1", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Normal schemes", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-normal}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:44bc4bd61fbc58368dc647efafc3b2d078f3fe667f5843e9faf9c2adff085963", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:93b96db2fb6e83a2ad99f788cd662351a76ec78906170808cf1b4379bf942996", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:033H:prose-0001", "parent_tag": "033H", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "risk_level": "R2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nRecall that a ring <MATH_0001> is said to be normal if all its local rings\nare normal domains,\nsee Algebra, Definition <REF_0001>.\nA normal domain is a domain which is integrally closed in its field\nof fractions, see\nAlgebra, Definition <REF_0002>.\nThus it makes sense to define a normal scheme as follows.\n\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "MATH_0001": "$R$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-definition-ring-normal}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-definition-domain-normal}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:46cb5a0eb1f6626beda70dd40157125d23b29bc402cf81a14e1e3797c41b2c48", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9e73ea5c9db5d170c46d865f220fbdbaab8c705c3dec431912c8cf993c5c5820", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e5fc7892ed5d3c89859f320312560ac7543d92ccd56c8b74f4e03c4acf0d532c"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:033I:statement", "parent_tag": "033H", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "definition", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "A scheme <MATH_0001> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>normal<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if and only if for all <MATH_0002> the local ring\n<MATH_0003> is a normal domain.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "MATH_0002": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-normal}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:545340ed163d29db36ad8b042d66548a951ec68c34c1121bbaaaa66a25461463", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e10153c512f9ce1392f7e6ffd99740d889aee8e87552b3a315262449974f079f", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0120189aa3c37c4ac5a3789b218f2e7ca8ebe57c9c2c0be76c70a652fb4fd573"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:033H:prose-0002", "parent_tag": "033H", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "risk_level": "R2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis seems to be the definition used in EGA, see <REF_0001>.\nSuppose <MATH_0001>, and <MATH_0002> is reduced. Then saying that <MATH_0003> is\nnormal is not equivalent to saying that <MATH_0004> is integrally closed in its\ntotal ring of fractions. However, if <MATH_0005> is Noetherian then this is the case\n(see Algebra, Lemma <REF_0002>).\n\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "REF_0001": "\\cite[0, 4.1.4]{EGA}", "MATH_0001": "$X = \\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0002": "$A$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$A$", "MATH_0005": "$A$", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-characterize-reduced-ring-normal}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:4e6f91d117c547d98a10f1eb80da187e16ca781425e289650eed1a99f1e68919", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cd9579400e4db60fbe3f9cd46c98961eaed094535f298dd53b5abe9806c671ac", "source_math_hash": "sha256:47ac1a80f0d8f3f1e338efd4fc82640b5fe1c136cc4d24aafcf6b716cd55e794"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:033J:statement", "parent_tag": "033H", "chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. The following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> The scheme <MATH_0002> is normal.\n<STRUCT_0003> For every affine open <MATH_0003> the ring <MATH_0004>\nis normal.\n<STRUCT_0004> There exists an affine open covering <MATH_0005> such that\neach <MATH_0006> is normal.\n<STRUCT_0005> There exists an open covering <MATH_0007>\nsuch that each open subscheme <MATH_0008> is normal.\n<STRUCT_0006>\nMoreover, if <MATH_0009> is normal then every open subscheme\nis normal.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "MATH_0003": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "MATH_0005": "$X = \\bigcup U_i$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U_i)$", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "MATH_0007": "$X = \\bigcup X_j$", "MATH_0008": "$X_j$", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}", "MATH_0009": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-locally-normal}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:6843d1f6e4b3106d5c401ebe411e7da3a6cb9696488db2a44c68d6b706c49cd8", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4daf4a369e8728444b54cbf382d5e5692787c79436e40e21a3e9f2980f8ae7d8", "source_math_hash": "sha256:555b2b125c46a99a2b385a173afe2abdca090cb0d8ed322725f9e75886cb4b24"}
